  "reason": "The records collectively support the broad strategy of altering HEA phase morphology and deformation behavior through thermal or thermomechanical processing. In particular, R10 concerns microstructural refinement in the closely related AlCoCrFeNi system; R7, R8, and R14 connect phase morphology, dual-phase structures, and coherency with mechanical response; and R1, R3, R18, R19, and R20 discuss interfaces or dislocation-related deformation mechanisms. However, none describes HPHT treatment with a hexahedron-anvil apparatus, pressure-induced conversion of FCC/B2 lamellae into a hierarchical coherent-interface pattern, or preferential FCC-to-B2 dislocation transfer. Thus, the literature points toward microstructure/interface engineering, but selecting HPHT and the specific coherent-interface mechanism would require a substantial new idea."
